    "https://faculty.tamu.edu/JobDetail.aspx?PositionId=191776&JobId=193452": {
      "title": "Academic Professional Track (Non-Tenure): Open Rank - Clinical (Prosthodontist)",
      "description": "Back to Listings Academic Professional Track (Non-Tenure): Open Rank - Clinical (Prosthodontist) Comprehensive Dentistry Location Dallas, Texas Open Date 10/5/2026 Position ID 191776 Description The Department of Comprehensive Dentistry at the Texas A&M University College of Dentistry invites applications for two full time 100% FTE, academic professional track (non-tenure) faculty position with an 11-month appointment Fall 2026, or negotiable. Applicants will be considered for the faculty titles of Clinical Assistant Professor, Clinical Associate Professor, or Clinical Professor; rank commensurate on review of qualifications. Faculty responsibilities include: - Clinical Coordination & Supervision : Coordinate clinical activities and supervise patient care to ensure excellence in service delivery and adherence to institutional standards. · Instruction & Course Leadership : Serve as instructor and/or course director for pre-doctoral courses, contributing to curriculum design and implementation. · Evidence-Based Teaching : Develop and deliver lectures that are grounded in current scientific evidence and best practices in dentistry. · Simulation & Laboratory Instruction : Teach in simulation clinics and laboratory settings, supporting students in developing foundational clinical competencies. · Clinical Education : Provide direct clinical instruction and mentorship during patient care, guiding students through procedures and decision-making. · Student Evaluation & Support : Assess students’ professionalism, clinical progress, and performance; offer regular academic and career counseling to foster growth and success. · Departmental Engagement : Participate in departmental initiatives, including committee service, faculty meetings, and collaborative academic activities Interested individuals should have a strong commitment to teaching and service. The opportunity for extramural private practice is available. Salary and academic rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience of the selected applicant. The Department of Comprehensive Dentistry at Texas A&M University College of Dentistry is a recognized leader. More information can be found at : Comprehensive Dentistry | College of Dentistry Qualifications · Candidate must have a DDS, DMD, or equivalent degree (e.g BDS) from a U.S. or foreign equivalent accredited dental school · Advanced education certificate in Prosthodontics from a U.S or foreign equivalent accredited dental school · Be eligible for dental licensure in the state of Texas · Candidate must have experience in all fields of general dentistry, strong clinical skills, a strong background in clinical practice, and be familiar with current dental technologies. Application Instructions Interested applicants must apply through the Texas A&M University faculty job board hosted by Interfolio at apply.interfolio.com/193452 and upload the following: 1) Curriculum Vitae, 2) Cover Letter 3) List of three references with full contact information including email addresses, and 4) Personal Statement include philosophy and plans for research, teaching, and service, as applicable. For questions related to this position, please contact Gracie Castillo at gracie.rangel@tamu.edu . Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier account and can send all application materials, including confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer. The University is aware that attracting and retaining exceptional faculty often depends on meeting the needs of two careers and therefore has a Dual Career Program ."
    },
    "https://faculty.tamu.edu/JobDetail.aspx?PositionId=190767&JobId=192522": {
      "title": "Academic Professional Track (Non-Tenure): Open Rank - Clinical or Instructional and Associate Dean of DVM Admissions and Student Recruitment",
      "description": "Back to Listings Academic Professional Track (Non-Tenure): Open Rank - Clinical or Instructional and Associate Dean of DVM Admissions and Student Recruitment College of Veterinary Medicine and Biomedical Sciences Location College Station, TX Open Date 9/16/2026 Position ID 190767 Description The College of Veterinary Medicine & Biomedical Sciences (VMBS) at Texas A&M University invites applications for the position of Associate Dean of DVM Admissions and Student Recruitment. This is a full-time, 11-month/year appointment faculty position with significant administrative duties (60% effort). The anticipated start date is fall 2026. Candidates seeking an Academic Professional Track (Non-Tenure) appointment will be considered for the faculty titles of Clinical Associate Professor, Clinical Professor, Instructional Associate Professor, or Instructional Professor commensurate with qualifications and professional interest. The departmental home for the successful candidate at VMBS will be determined based on the applicant’s area of expertise and experience. Responsibilities for this position as a faculty member include teaching in the DVM curriculum (10-30% effort), providing academic service to the college and Texas A&M University (10% effort), and contributing to research/scholarship (5-25%). Opportunities to contribute to patient care in the Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital are also available. The Associate Dean of DVM Admissions and Student Recruitment is responsible for providing strategic leadership for admissions and student recruitment within the Doctor of Veterinary Medicine (DVM) program. Reporting directly to the Dean of VMBS, the Associate Dean serves as a member of the college leadership team and collaborates with faculty, staff, and external partners to advance VMBS strategic priorities in education and student success. The Associate Dean will lead a comprehensive and mission-aligned approach to admissions and recruitment, ensuring excellence, fairness, and compliance in all processes. This role is central to shaping the DVM student body and enhancing student success through student recruitment and evidence-based admissions processes. Key Responsibilities Admissions Leadership and Operations Provide strategic oversight of holistic review processes for DVM applicants Assess ongoing admissions processes and investigate emerging selection methodologies Lead and guide the DVM Selections Committee in evaluating, interviewing, and ranking applicants Direct Admissions Office operations, including TMDSAS application management, interview coordination, and final selections Provide reporting for and ensure compliance with COE accreditation standards and all state and university regulations Student Recruitment and Pipeline Development Develop and implement recruitment strategies aligned with VMBS and university missions Strengthen outreach and pipeline programs to attract highly qualified applicants Student Financial Support and Advancement Provide leadership for financial aid and scholarship programs for incoming students Partner with development efforts to enhance student scholarship fundraising About VMBS and Texas A&M: For over 110 years, the VMBS has been a leader in veterinary education and biomedical discovery, serving the people and industries of Texas and beyond. With 180 students per class, it is home to one of the country's largest DVM programs. The VMBS is ranked #3 in the United States and #5 in the world in the 2026 Quacquarelli Symonds (QS) World University Rankings in veterinary science. For more information about the college visit: https://vetmed.tamu.edu Texas A&M is a Tier 1 research university and one of the largest universities in the United States, with more than 4,300 faculty members and the third-largest student body in the Nation, according to the 2025 U.S. News and World Report. Texas A&M is a flagship land grant, sea grant, and space grant university, and a member of the prestigious Association of American Universities (AAU). About the Bryan/College Station Metropolitan Area: The Bryan/College Station metro area (“Aggieland”) has a population of over 250,000 and is among the 15 fastest-growing metro areas in the United States, according to the U.S. Census Bureau. Residents enjoy a vibrant economy that Forbes and WalletHub rank as one of the best areas in the United States for job growth and start-up companies. Residents also enjoy a low cost of living (including no state income taxes), short commute times, and a vast network of parks (nearly 100), walking paths, greenspaces, and high-quality golf courses. Moreover, College Station is recognized as having some of the strongest public schools in Texas, as well as a very low crime rate and excellent health care. For these and many other reasons, College Station has consistently been rated as one of the best college towns in the United States. For a list of College Station’s recognitions and rankings in a variety of social and economic categories, see https://www.cstx.gov/our_community/recognitions__rankings . Qualifications Required: DVM or equivalent degree Clinical practice experience in the U.S. or Canada Minimum of five years of teaching experience in veterinary medical education Demonstrated leadership and administrative experience Excellent organizational and communication skills Preferred: Board certification in an AVMA-recognized specialty or a PhD degree Experience in admissions, recruitment, or academic administration Application Instructions Interested applicants for the position must apply through the Texas A&M University faculty job board hosted by Interfolio at: For Academic Professional Track (Non-Tenure) position: https://apply.interfolio.com/192522 For Tenured position: https://apply.interfolio.com/192526 Applicants must upload the following: 1. Cover letter 2. Curriculum vitae 3. Personal statement to include philosophy and plans for teaching, service, research/scholarship, patient care, as applicable 4. Contact information for at least three (3) references to solicit letters of recommendation Questions can be sent to the attention of Lisa Ashorn, Senior Administrative Coordinator ( lashorn@tamu.edu ). Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier account and can send all application materials, including confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer. The University is aware that attracting and retaining exceptional faculty often depends on meeting the needs of two careers and therefore has a Dual Career Program ."
    },
